	"Name": "Search - LLM - Upstream Errors Over Time by Model [chart]",
	"Description": "Upstream failures over time, broken out by model, so a provider incident is easy to separate from a client bug.\n\nThe LLM ingester attaches its fields as intrinsic enumerated values, so the query declares the ones it needs on the `intrinsic` extraction module in the tag block. The `intrinsic` module filters on equality only -- it has no `<`, `>`, `<=`, or `>=` -- so the `>= 400` test is an `eval` with an `int()` cast after the extraction.",
